   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT granting retroactive membership in the New York state and local employees' retirement system to Joseph J. Maltese",
    "basePrintNo": "S6730",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6730-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6730                Revised 1/18/18\n\nSPONSOR: LANZA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act granting retroactive membership in the New York\nstate and local employees' retirement system to Joseph J. Maltese\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill will grant Tier 1 status to Joseph J. Maltese, an employee of\nthe New York State unified court system, by changing his date of member-\nship to February 2, 1970, his first date of employment with the New York\nCity civil court.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one allows Joseph J. Maltese to become a member of the NY state\nand local employees' retirement system on February 2, 1970, if he files\nan application with the state Comptroller's office within one year of\nthis act becoming law. This will give him Tier 1 status in the NY state\nand local employees' retirement system.\n\nSection two says the New York State Unified Court System will pay for\nthe past costs of implementing this bill.\n\nSection three is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nJoseph J. Maltese is an Associate Justice of the Appellate Division,\nSecond Department of the New York State Supreme Court and is employed by\nthe New York State Unified Court System. Judge Maltese currently holds\nTier 2 status with a membership date of March 25, 1974. Judge Maltese\nwas previously employed from February 2, 1970 through September 4, 1970\nas a full-time court assistant with the New York City Civil Court, but\nwas not offered membership in the New York City employees' retirement\nsystem at the time. From June 7, 1971 through September 3, 1971 was\nemployed as a legal intern with the New York State Office of the Attor-\nney General, but was not offered membership in the New York State and\nLocal Employees' Retirement System at that time. Judge Maltese should\nhave been offered membership in the New York City Employees' Retirement\nSystem when initially employed by them. This bill would correct this\nerror by providing him with retroactive membership in the retirement\nsystem.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017: S.6730 - Referred to Rules / A.8411 - Referred to Governmental\nEmployees\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect immediately.\n",
